Q: Parent and child gestures not firing together in Flutter A: <p>By changing the widget layout it is possible to achieve the requested behaviour:</p>
<pre><code>import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() =&gt; runApp(MyApp());

class MyApp extends StatelessWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return MaterialApp(
      home: Scaffold(
        body: Stack(
          children: [
            Center(
              child: GestureDetector(
                onTap: () =&gt; debugPrint(&quot;Red container tapped&quot;),
                child: Container(width: 500, height: 400, color: Colors.red),
              ),
            ),
            Center(
              child: GestureDetector(
                onTap: () =&gt; debugPrint(&quot;Blue container tapped&quot;),
                child: Container(width: 300, height: 200, color: Colors.blue),
              ),
            ),

          ],
        ),
      ),
    );
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Clicking on the red outer container and then on the blue inner container produces the following output:</p>
<pre><code>Red container tapped
Blue container tapped
</code></pre>
